{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And Israel sent messengers.</b> Elsewhere the sending is attributed to Moshe, as it says ״וָאֶשְׁלַח מַלְאָכִים מִמִּדְבַּר קְדֵמוֹת״ (Deuteronomy 2), and likewise ״וַיִּשְׁלַח מֹשֶׁה מַלְאָכִים מִקָּדֵשׁ אֶל מֶלֶךְ אֱדוֹם״ (Numbers 20), and regarding Yiftach it says (Judges 11) ״וַיִּשְׁלַח יִשְׂרָאֵל מַלְאָכִים אֶל מֶלֶךְ אֱדוֹם״ etc. These verses need one another — this one closes and that one opens: Moshe is Israel, and Israel are Moshe — to tell you that the leader of the generation is like the entire generation, for the leader is everything (Tanchuma)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:12:03.671649344Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}